Could `sum_q` be computed only when `residual_empty` is true? In `e028861`, the target reduction also runs on nonempty-residual and bonus paths.

I ran an AI-assisted kernel comparison (FP32, vocabulary 248,320; 11 paired rounds × 20 launches per variant, resets excluded). Median within-round time ratios to the fixed baseline were:

| Batch | Path | Baseline | #42534 | #42850 | Conditional |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | Nonempty residual | 1.000 | 0.994 | 1.260 | 0.999 |
| 1 | Bonus after acceptance | 1.000 | 0.990 | 1.338 | 1.012 |
| 8 | Nonempty residual | 1.000 | 0.926 | 1.063 | 0.981 |
| 8 | Bonus after acceptance | 1.000 | 0.993 | 1.177 | 1.008 |
| 32 | Nonempty residual | 1.000 | 0.997 | 1.002 | 1.009 |
| 32 | Bonus after acceptance | 1.000 | 0.998 | 1.013 | 1.003 |

At batch 1, #42850 adds about 23 µs on each path (26%/34%), while the conditional variant stays near baseline in this session. It matched #42850's valid predictions and acceptance fields on 13 fixtures, including boundary coins, but takes longer on forced-empty inputs.

These are synthetic, single-session timings on one RTX 3070, not serving benchmarks.

[Reproduction bundle](https://github.com/akatsukiwork0320/sglang-speculative-sampling-repro/tree/8348ca2e6d0ea2f5e6e324ad853e4c71066c9487) contains the harness, raw results, full comparisons and pinned dependencies. The proposed diff and measurement details follow.

<details>
<summary>Measurement details and forced-empty tradeoff</summary>

The baseline header is byte-identical to [main at 1638c5d](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/1638c5d6999525a4ae705120a2ca92e6adf0264e/python/sglang/kernels/jit/include/sgl_kernel/speculative/sampling.cuh). PR heads are `645faa1` (#42534) and `e028861` (#42850).

The harness uses reused buffers, a fixed draft=3/speculative=2 tree, and shuffled variant order within rounds. CUDA events exclude scratch resets. GPU clocks varied. Batch-8 nonempty residual timings were variable; batch 32 shows no useful common-path gain here. All 12 cells, including the vocabulary-32,768 control, and IQRs are included. Ratios are formed within rounds before taking the median.

| Batch | Path | Baseline | #42534 | #42850 | Conditional |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | Forced empty residual | 1.000 | 0.998 | 0.588 | 0.713 |
| 8 | Forced empty residual | 1.000 | 0.995 | 0.582 | 0.784 |
| 32 | Forced empty residual | 1.000 | 1.004 | 0.530 | 0.779 |

The baseline produces invalid outputs on forced-empty inputs; its time is only a cost reference. #42534 uses a different fallback rule. Conditional/#42850 time ratios on this path are 1.213/1.348/1.526 at batches 1/8/32. Mixed batches and production fallback frequency were not measured. The 13 matching fixtures establish agreement on those inputs, not a general equivalence proof.

</details>

<details>
<summary>Proposed diff against #42850 at e028861</summary>

The residual sum is broadcast before the block-uniform branch. The conditional target reduction retains the original tile order. This patch uses the upstream namespace; the measured harness gave the candidate a separate namespace for side-by-side compilation. The functional code is the same. Source hashes and modification notices are retained in the reproduction archive.

```diff
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/jit/include/sgl_kernel/speculative/sampling.cuh
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/jit/include/sgl_kernel/speculative/sampling.cuh
@@ -103,10 +103,8 @@
 
   // sample from relu(target_probs - draft_probs)
   DType sum_relu_q_minus_p(0);
-  DType sum_q(0);
   vec_t<DType, VEC_SIZE> q_vec, p_vec;
   DType relu_q_minus_p[VEC_SIZE];
-  DType q_arr[VEC_SIZE];
   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < ceil_div(d, BLOCK_THREADS * VEC_SIZE); ++i) {
     q_vec.fill(DType(0));
     p_vec.fill(DType(0));
@@ -120,12 +118,9 @@
 #pragma unroll
     for (uint32_t j = 0; j < VEC_SIZE; ++j) {
       relu_q_minus_p[j] = max(q_vec[j] - p_vec[j], DType(0));
-      q_arr[j] = q_vec[j];
     }
     sum_relu_q_minus_p += BlockReduce<DType, BLOCK_THREADS, REDUCE_ALGORITHM>(temp_storage.block_prim.reduce)
                               .Sum<VEC_SIZE>(relu_q_minus_p);
-    __syncthreads();
-    sum_q += BlockReduce<DType, BLOCK_THREADS, REDUCE_ALGORITHM>(temp_storage.block_prim.reduce).Sum<VEC_SIZE>(q_arr);
     __syncthreads();
   }
   if (tx == 0) {
@@ -137,12 +132,6 @@
   __syncthreads();
   sum_relu_q_minus_p = temp_storage.block_aggregate.value;
   __syncthreads();
-  if (tx == 0) {
-    temp_storage.block_aggregate.value = sum_q;
-  }
-  __syncthreads();
-  sum_q = temp_storage.block_aggregate.value;
-
   // The residual relu(q - p) can be empty: every token the target gives mass to was a
   // rejected draft (so p == q there). That happens when the coin equals the target's
   // renormalized mass (e.g. a one-token nucleus of 1 - 2^-24 and coin == 1 - 2^-24,
@@ -151,7 +140,33 @@
   // token id d - 1 - a token with zero target probability. Sample from the target
   // distribution itself in that case.
   const bool residual_empty = !(sum_relu_q_minus_p > DType(0));
-  DType u = coin * (residual_empty ? sum_q : sum_relu_q_minus_p);
+  DType sampling_mass = sum_relu_q_minus_p;
+  if (residual_empty) {
+    // The broadcast residual makes this branch uniform across the block.
+    // Keep the original target reduction's tile order and per-tile algorithm.
+    DType sum_q(0);
+    DType q_arr[VEC_SIZE];
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < ceil_div(d, BLOCK_THREADS * VEC_SIZE); ++i) {
+      q_vec.fill(DType(0));
+      if ((i * BLOCK_THREADS + tx) * VEC_SIZE < d) {
+        q_vec.load(target_probs + cur_prob_offset + i * BLOCK_THREADS * VEC_SIZE + tx * VEC_SIZE);
+      }
+#pragma unroll
+      for (uint32_t j = 0; j < VEC_SIZE; ++j) {
+        q_arr[j] = q_vec[j];
+      }
+      sum_q += BlockReduce<DType, BLOCK_THREADS, REDUCE_ALGORITHM>(temp_storage.block_prim.reduce).Sum<VEC_SIZE>(q_arr);
+      __syncthreads();
+    }
+    if (tx == 0) {
+      temp_storage.block_aggregate.value = sum_q;
+    }
+    __syncthreads();
+    sampling_mass = temp_storage.block_aggregate.value;
+    // Complete the broadcast before the sampling scan reuses shared storage.
+    __syncthreads();
+  }
+  DType u = coin * sampling_mass;
 
   DType aggregate_relu_q_minus_p(0);
   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < ceil_div(d, BLOCK_THREADS * VEC_SIZE); ++i) {
```

</details>

